# app Hermes plugins shipped in the agent image

Six plugins, each closing a measured gap in upstream Hermes. None is
decoration: before removing one, check the retirement condition below against
the CURRENT upstream source — enumeration of features in release notes is not
evidence; the adapter code is.

Last full audit against upstream main: **2026-08-19** (v2026.8.18, ~30k-line
gateway grepped, quotes verified). Verdict: **all six gaps still open** for the
Mattermost path. Details per plugin:

# image build warnings {#image_build_warnings}

Hermes' installer probes ffmpeg and used to warn after the base apt lists had
already been removed. That warning was functional, not cosmetic: cloud STT
transcoding, silence trimming, duration probes and Opus TTS could degrade. The
base image now installs the exact Noble package `ffmpeg=7:6.1.1-3ubuntu5`
before invoking the installer.

The npm install currently emits a `node-domexception` deprecation from an
upstream transitive dependency. It is retained because none of our direct pins
select it and the installed CLIs pass their executable smoke checks. npm may
also report packages whose lifecycle scripts are restricted; the image's
explicit Claude SDK binary check and CLI smoke checks are the authority. Do not
globally enable lifecycle scripts: that would widen build-time code execution
for every dependency. Revisit the individual allowlist only when one of those
checks demonstrates a missing artifact.

* **conversation-key** — puts Hermes' session id on the wire as
  `x-conversation-id`. Upstream custom providers gained only STATIC
  `extra_headers` (fixed per profile, `normalize_extra_headers`), nothing per
  session. Retire when Hermes sends a per-conversation id natively, or when
  acp2api keys sessions from ACP `_meta` end to end.
* **mention-on-edit** — adapter still handles only `event == "posted"`
  (`plugins/platforms/mattermost/adapter.py`); `post_edited` appears nowhere.
  Scoped to HUMAN authors on purpose: an agent's progress bubble once woke a
  colleague mid-edit (three faults from one cause). Retire when upstream
  processes `post_edited`.
* **untagged-routing** — upstream now has `ThreadParticipationTracker`
  ("follow-up messages in bot-participated threads need no mention") wired
  into **Discord, Slack, Matrix only**, plus `profile_routing.py` which maps
  already-accepted messages to profiles and claims nothing. The Mattermost
  adapter uses neither, and room-ownership (rule 4) exists nowhere upstream.
  Keep for Mattermost; for a Discord/Slack/Matrix fleet compare against the
  tracker before porting the binding. Upstreaming a patch that wires the
  tracker into the Mattermost adapter would retire rule 2 (thread ownership)
  only — rules 1, 3, 4 (humans-only, solo group DM, room owners) stay ours.
* **reasoning-live** — `reasoning_callback` is still assigned only by the CLI;
  zero occurrences under `gateway/`. Chat platforms drop reasoning deltas
  without this. Retire when the gateway subscribes.
* **steer-into-turn** — upstream `steer()` still only queues for the next
  model call, which never comes when one call is the whole ACP turn. The one
  native exception is Codex app-server's `turn/steer` — irrelevant here, the
  brains sit behind acp2api as `provider: custom`. Retire if Hermes grows an
  HTTP steering sidechannel for custom providers.
* **trace-to-card** — also supplies `delete_message`, which the Mattermost
  adapter still lacks (google_chat/slack/telegram have it); without it the
  gateway silently disables `display.cleanup_progress`
  (`base.py`: TTL cleanup skipped when the adapter does not override).

Note when reading upstream: PyPI `hermes-agent` (0.19.0, 2026-07-20) is a
month and several releases behind main — audit against main or the latest tag,
never against pip.

# bad Patterns these plugins already paid for {#plugin_traps}

* A monkeypatched method must present the WRAPPED signature — Hermes inspects
  it; a `**kwargs` wrapper advertises parameters the real method lacks and
  every call dies in a caught-and-logged handler, invisibly.
* Patch the adapter class found via `sys.modules`, never by importing its file
  path — plugins load under `hermes_plugins.<slug>`, so a path import yields a
  second, unrelated class that patches cleanly and changes nothing.
* A module run through `spec_from_file_location` must be in `sys.modules`
  BEFORE `exec_module`, or `@dataclass` dies on a NoneType error naming
  neither the file nor dataclasses.
* Log at WARNING or above — this container emits nothing quieter, and a
  refusal logged at INFO is indistinguishable from a plugin that never loaded.
* Anything that rewrites the final post must patch BOTH delivery paths (edit
  of the streamed preview AND `send`) — patching only `edit_message` passes
  tests and never fires in production.
